                      (    forth6809.asm):02001         ; TSTSLASHZ - unit test for SLASH, divide-by-zero case. n2 = 0.
                      (    forth6809.asm):02002         ; Verifies THROW -10 fires (per this system's documented ANS
                      (    forth6809.asm):02003         ; behavior for a zero divisor) and that CATCH's own depth-
                      (    forth6809.asm):02004         ; restoration contract holds (net 0 change across the JSR CATCH,
                      (    forth6809.asm):02005         ; xt's slot effectively replaced by the throw code). Per CATCH's
                      (    forth6809.asm):02006         ; own spec, the i*x arguments' VALUES are explicitly unspecified
                      (    forth6809.asm):02007         ; after a catch, not just untested here - the final, unconditional
                      (    forth6809.asm):02008         ; stack restore discards them without needing to know how many
                      (    forth6809.asm):02009         ; there are.
                      (    forth6809.asm):02010         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
