DF41 DD00             (    forth6809.asm):05867                  STD   STATE     ; below, running on EVERY line - including
                      (    forth6809.asm):05868                                   ; lines in the middle of a colon definition
                      (    forth6809.asm):05869                                   ; that spans more than one line of input.
                      (    forth6809.asm):05870                                   ; COLON (sets STATE=-1) and SEMI (sets
                      (    forth6809.asm):05871                                   ; STATE=0, after checking CSP) are the
                      (    forth6809.asm):05872                                   ; correct, sole places STATE should change
                      (    forth6809.asm):05873                                   ; during normal operation - the old QLOOP
                      (    forth6809.asm):05874                                   ; reset was a third, redundant one that
                      (    forth6809.asm):05875                                   ; silently dropped back to interpret mode
                      (    forth6809.asm):05876                                   ; every time QUERY read a new line,
                      (    forth6809.asm):05877                                   ; regardless of whether ";" had actually
                      (    forth6809.asm):05878                                   ; been reached. A colon definition split
                      (    forth6809.asm):05879                                   ; across multiple lines would have every
                      (    forth6809.asm):05880                                   ; word on every line after the first
                      (    forth6809.asm):05881                                   ; interpreted (and, for anything with a
                      (    forth6809.asm):05882                                   ; stack effect, executed) instead of
                      (    forth6809.asm):05883                                   ; compiled - "TRUE" pushing TRUEV onto the
