                      (    forth6809.asm):09834                      ; the bare registered name (via SEARCHW), which found
                      (    forth6809.asm):09835                      ; "girl" and replaced only that span, leaving surrounding
                      (    forth6809.asm):09836                      ; "%...%" delimiters untouched in the output - and never
                      (    forth6809.asm):09837                      ; returned the substitution count ANS requires as a
                      (    forth6809.asm):09838                      ; third stack item. Per the ANS spec (forth-standard.org/
                      (    forth6809.asm):09839                      ; standard/string/SUBSTITUTE), SUBSTITUTE must scan for
                      (    forth6809.asm):09840                      ; text between '%' (ASCII $25) delimiter pairs
                      (    forth6809.asm):09841                      ; specifically: "%%" collapses to a single '%' (count
                      (    forth6809.asm):09842                      ; unchanged); a name matching the REPLACES registration
                      (    forth6809.asm):09843                      ; has the ENTIRE "%name%" span - delimiters included -
                      (    forth6809.asm):09844                      ; replaced by the substitution text (count incremented);
                      (    forth6809.asm):09845                      ; a non-matching name is passed through unchanged,
                      (    forth6809.asm):09846                      ; delimiters and all (count unchanged); an unpaired
                      (    forth6809.asm):09847                      ; trailing '%' with no closing delimiter passes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):09848                      ; residue through unchanged. Confirmed via MAME testing
                      (    forth6809.asm):09849                      ; against a real template. GLOBALS is fully packed
                      (    forth6809.asm):09850                      ; (256/256), so this reuses MSCR/MSCR2/MSCR3/MSCR4
                      (    forth6809.asm):09851                      ; (confirmed untouched by SUBCOPY) rather than adding
